      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "id": "heating_energy_calculator",
      "content": "## Heating Energy Calculator\n\nCalculate the energy required to heat a solid using: **q = cp × m × ΔT**",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "specific_heat",
          "label": "Specific Heat (cp)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 2,
          "unit": "kJ/kgK"
        },
        {
          "id": "mass",
          "label": "Mass (m)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 10,
          "unit": "kg"
        },
        {
          "id": "temp_diff",
          "label": "Temperature Difference (ΔT)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 30,
          "unit": "K or °C"
        },
        {
          "id": "time",
          "label": "Heating Time (optional)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 3600,
          "unit": "seconds"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "heat_required",
          "label": "Heat Required (q)",
          "formula": "inputs.specific_heat * inputs.mass * inputs.temp_diff",
          "unit": "kJ",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "power_required",
          "label": "Power Required (P)",
          "formula": "(inputs.specific_heat * inputs.mass * inputs.temp_diff) / inputs.time",
          "unit": "kW",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "formulas_info",
      "content": "## Formulas\n\n### Heating Energy\n**q = cp × m × ΔT**\n\nWhere:\n- **q** = heat required (kJ)\n- **cp** = specific heat (kJ/kg K or kJ/kg °C)\n- **m** = mass (kg)\n- **ΔT** = temperature difference (K or °C)\n\n### Power Required\n**P = q / t**\n\nWhere:\n- **P** = power (kW)\n- **t** = time (seconds)\n\n### Unit Conversion\n- 1 Btu/lbm°F = 4.187 kJ/kg K = 1 kcal/kg°C\n- T (°C) = 5/9(T (°F) - 32)\n- T (°F) = (T (°C))(9/5) + 32"
    }
  ]
}